.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
.TH SHULID 8 "August 2026" "shuli" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
shulid \- WiFi authentication daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shulid
.RI [ config ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shulid
is a pure-Rust WiFi authentication daemon implementing
WPA3-Personal (SAE), WPA2-Personal (PSK), OWE (RFC 8110),
and open authentication, including 802.11r/802.11v roaming.
It performs the full authentication flow in userspace: scan,
authentication, association, 4-way handshake, and key
installation via nl80211.  Data-frame encryption (CCMP) is
handled by the kernel once keys are installed.
.PP
On successful authentication the link is brought up with the
configured IP settings (static, DHCPv4, IPv6 SLAAC), and
.B shulid
holds the connection, handling group rekeys (in userspace or
offloaded to the driver when supported) and roaming.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I config
Path to the YAML configuration file.  Default:
.IR /etc/shuli/config.yml .
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is YAML, one entry per SSID:
.PP
.RS
.nf
---
version: 1
wifis:
  - ssid: Test-WIFI
    password: "12345678"
    interface: any
    roaming: true
    roaming_threshold: -70
    sae_pwe: auto
    wowlan: true
    dns:
      nameservers:
        - 192.0.2.1
    ipv4:
      auto: true
    ipv6:
      auto: true
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B ssid
Network name to scan for and connect to (required).
.TP
.B password
Passphrase for WPA2-Personal / WPA3-Personal networks.
Omit for open networks.
.TP
.B interface
Interface to bind to; \fBany\fR (or omitted) picks the first
WiFi NIC.  Entries sharing an interface share one connection
engine; different interfaces connect concurrently.
.TP
.B roaming
Signal-triggered roaming (default \fBtrue\fR); BTM (802.11v)
requests are always honoured.
.TP
.B roaming_threshold
Signal level (dBm) below which the client scans for roam
candidates (default \fB-70\fR).
.TP
.B sae_pwe
SAE PWE derivation: \fBauto\fR (default), \fBh2e\fR, or
\fBhnp\fR.
.TP
.B wowlan
Wake-on-WLAN: arm the wiphy's Disconnect / GTK-rekey-failure
triggers while connected so the device can wake the host on
suspend.  Default \fBfalse\fR (opt-in).
.TP
.B dns.nameservers / dns.searches
DNS servers and search domains to write to
.IR /etc/resolv.conf .
.TP
.B ipv4 / ipv6
Per-family config: \fBauto: true\fR for DHCPv4 / IPv6 SLAAC,
or \fBauto: false\fR with \fBaddress\fR and \fBgateway\fR for
static configuration.
.SH ETHERNETS
Wired 802.1X ports are configured in a top-level
.B ethernets
section.  Each entry names an Ethernet NIC and carries an
.B eap
block plus the same
.B dns / ipv4 / ipv6
settings as WiFi entries:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ethernets:
  - name: eth0
    eap:
      identity: user@example.org
      ca_cert: /etc/shuli/ca.pem
      client_cert: /etc/shuli/client.pem
      client_key: /etc/shuli/client.key
      server_name: radius.example.org
    ipv4:
      auto: true
.fi
.RE
.PP
There is no association, 4-way handshake, or key installation on
wired links: EAP-TLS runs directly over EAPOL (ethertype 0x888E) and
EAP-Success authorizes the port before the IP config is applied.
.SH SYSTEMD
The package ships
.I packaging/shulid.service
which starts
.B shulid
as root (required for nl80211/rtnetlink, the raw DHCPv4
socket, IPv6 sysctls, and \fI/etc/resolv.conf\fR).  Install
it and the default config with:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo install -Dm644 packaging/shulid.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo install -Dm644 examples/config.yml /etc/shuli/config.yml
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now shulid
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/shuli/config.yml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/shulid
Daemon binary.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/shulid.service
Installed systemd unit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Cleanly disconnect from the AP, clear WoWLAN triggers, and
exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Connection was established and held until a shutdown signal.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error (configuration, netlink, or shutdown before
connection was established).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hostapd (8),
.BR wpa_supplicant (8),
.BR iwd (8)
